 r"I am writing to apply for the Data, AI \& Digital Engineering Analyst Graduate Programme at Alpha FMC, on the Data Engineering track. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. The role you describe, working with client teams to turn fragmented data into something trustworthy for reporting, decisions and AI, is the kind of work I enjoy most.",

 r"What draws me to Alpha is the combination of consulting and hands-on delivery. I like working directly with the people who own a problem, understanding what they need, and then building the thing that solves it, rather than handing over a slide. I am also interested in how insurers and asset managers are starting to use AI on top of their data, because that only works when the data underneath is clean, well-modelled and well-governed.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I query large merchant and transaction tables in SQL and Python and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. A large part of the job is agreeing one definition of each metric and checking the data behind it before anyone acts on it. When my supervisor asked me to configure a merchant campaign by hand, I used Claude Code to build an AI agent with a validation step to check its accuracy, which cut the time the task took by around 40 to 50 percent and is now used by my team and partner teams.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked on a client engagement for a pharmaceutical company. I built a Python pipeline that called six LLM APIs with retrieval and search augmentation and scored more than 2,400 responses, built a regex and LLM extraction pipeline that turned 4,800 free-text patient threads into structured data, and presented the results to the client, who adopted our benchmark as its acceptance standard. Working in a regulated healthcare setting taught me to treat data quality and documentation as part of the deliverable. My MSc dissertation added experience of engineering features from 458,840 UK Biobank records across several time points.",

 r"I would bring Alpha strong SQL and Python, experience building data and LLM pipelines, a careful approach to data quality, and experience working directly with clients. I have a 2:1 from Imperial, I am available to start in August 2027, and I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029 without sponsorship. I am based in London.",

 r"Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how I could contribute to Alpha's Data \& AI team.",
